    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n`starter.sections.telescope` is very convenient, but allowing customized commands would be best.",
    "closed_at": "2022-03-20T19:50:26Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nAt first glance, I am not really convinced that this adds much non-trivial functionality compared to added code base complexity. Also it creates names identical to `Telescope` action. Probably, having `key` represent `name` might be better, but this also has hidden inconvenience of user not being able to define order of items (`pairs` iterates in pre-defined order of keys).\r\n\r\nDo you think that having to do manual set of items is so bad that it needs this functionality?",
            "created_at": "2022-03-20T15:01:17Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/54#issuecomment-1073269490",
            "id": 1073269490,
